.TH COASTLINE-RUN-SCRIPT 1 "2026-11-01" "Coastline @CMAKE_PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coastline-run-script \- drive Coastline with scripted input and screenshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coastline
.RI [ options ]
.B run-script
.I SCRIPT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each nonblank line of SCRIPT specifies one command.
A # starts a comment.
Frame numbers start at 1.
Commands supplement ordinary input.
Global options precede run-script.
Use \-\-data-dir for an isolated data directory and \-\-config for a separate
INI file.
.PP
Scripts operate setup when game data is unavailable and keyboard, text, or
mouse input is supplied.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B autopilot
Let the computer drive the first car.
Applies from the start without a frame prefix.
.TP
.BI "screenshot-every " N
Capture every N frames.
N must be positive.
Applies from the start without a frame prefix.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " "press BUTTON " "[FRAMES [PORT]]"
Press a controller button for FRAMES frames, defaulting to 6.
PORT is 1 through 4 and defaults to 1.
BUTTON is a, b, z, start, l, r, up, down, left, right, cu, cd, cl, or cr.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " "key KEY " "[FRAMES]"
Press the SDL key KEY for FRAMES frames, defaulting to 6.
Use SDL key names such as Return, Escape, or F.
Ctrl, Alt, Shift, and Gui select left-side modifier keys.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " "type TEXT"
Type the remainder of the line as UTF-8.
The special values <backspace> and <enter> press editing keys.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " "mouse X Y " "[BUTTON [FRAMES]]"
Position the pointer on the 320x240 logical input surface.
BUTTON is none, left, or right and defaults to none.
FRAMES defaults to 1.
Setup maps the same coordinates to its text grid.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " screenshot
Capture the current frame.
.TP
.IB "FRAME " quit
Exit after the specified frame.
If several quit commands are present, the earliest applies.
.SH CAPTURES
PNG files are written below screenshots in the data directory,
with filenames such as frame-000060.png.
Capture runs advance front-end animation at a fixed 60 frames per second.
Captures include game presentation filters and enabled full statistics.
Full statistics use output resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
Save the following commands as test.txt.
.nf
60 press a
180 press a
240 screenshot
300 quit
.fi
.PP
Run the script with the following command.
.nf
coastline \-\-config ./test.ini run-script test.txt
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a normal exit.
A nonzero status indicates an unreadable script, invalid command, or startup
failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coastline (1),
.BR coastline-import (1)
